      "description": "Watch Kilmarnock vs Dundee Utd highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. Rugby Park set the stage for a compelling Scottish Premiership encounter on August 29, 2026, as Kilmarnock hosted a confident Dundee United side. With both teams looking to climb the league standings, the match promised a high-octane battle under the lights. A Clinical First Half Display The match ignited early on, with intensity levels high from the opening whistle. Dundee United ’s Bert Esselink received a yellow card within ten minutes, signaling the physical nature of the contest. However, the visitors quickly turned their aggression into goals. In the 12th minute, Mehdi Merghem delivered a perfectly weighted assist for Emmanuel Agyei , who finished clinically to put the visitors ahead. Kilmarnock faced further adversity when Robbie Deas was forced off early through injury, replaced by George Stanger . The momentum stayed firmly with the visitors, and in the 36th minute, Zachary Sapsford calmly converted a penalty to double the lead. Dundee United Extend Their Advantage Just as Kilmarnock attempted to reorganize, they were hit with a third blow before the break. In the 41st minute, the creative Mehdi Merghem notched his second assist of the day, setting up Will Ferry for a strike that effectively took the game away from the hosts. A flurry of yellow cards followed, as Joe Hugill and Zachary Sapsford were both cautioned in a heated end to the first half. The visitors headed into the tunnel with a commanding three-goal lead, leaving the home side with a mountain to climb in the second period. Second Half Dominance and Final Whistle Kilmarnock introduced several fresh faces at the start of the second half, including Jamie Brandon and Djenairo Daniels , in a desperate bid to spark a comeback. Despite the tactical shifts, Dundee United remained composed and continued to threaten on the counter. The fourth goal arrived in the 77th minute when substitute Jesse Randall found the back of the net, assisted by the industrious Will Ferry . The final stages of the match were well-managed by the visitors, and despite a late yellow card for Bailey Rice , the result was never in doubt. The referee blew for full-time at 0-4, marking a significant statement victory for Dundee United on the road."
